1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:07,130
Since 20 October 2026, Singapore companies no longer need public opening hours at their registered office.

2
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:12,340
But company records must still be produced for inspection on reasonable notice.

3
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:19,250
Under the Corporate and Accounting Laws Amendment Act 2025, ACRA removed the minimum opening hours.

4
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:27,180
Once someone gives reasonable notice, records must be available for at least two hours on each relevant business day.

5
00:00:27,530 --> 00:00:30,830
Address changes must still be filed within 14 days.

6
00:00:31,330 --> 00:00:35,530
That shifts the burden from staffing an office to finding records fast.

7
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:42,670
Common gaps are unindexed minute books, scattered share transfer forms, and registers that cannot be found quickly.

8
00:00:43,170 --> 00:00:54,550
To get ready, list what can be inspected, locate every copy, scan the paper backlog to searchable PDF with an index, keep one controlled source, and test a request.

9
00:00:55,050 --> 00:01:03,330
IRAS also expects records to be kept for at least five years, so inspection readiness and retention overlap for most active files.

10
00:01:03,830 --> 00:01:08,400
